MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next addition because I could monitor my door alongside the Echo devices I already use, provided the setup works for my home.",
    "The Alexa speakers, Mac-compatible Bluetooth keyboard and removable storage reflect things I have bought before, so their intended uses feel familiar and relevant."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The memory modules and internal SSD assume I am upgrading a computer, but I have no such project planned or confirmed hardware compatibility; buying peripherals and external storage does not establish that need.",
    "AirPods do not address a current need, while another Dot or keyboard would duplicate devices I recently bought. The compact keyboard also leaves out the numeric keypad on my recent full-size keyboard."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My computer-accessory purchases seem to have been taken as interest in computer components generally, although installing memory or an internal drive involves a different purpose and compatibility requirements.",
    "My repeated Echo purchases seem to suggest I want more Alexa devices immediately, although another speaker or a whole camera bundle needs a specific use beyond belonging to the same setup."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Dot and full-size keyboard purchases matter because those needs may already be covered; an accessory or a new function can be more useful now than another version of the device.",
    "I need a concrete use and suitable compatibility before choosing hardware: the doorbell offers a clear new function, but a 512GB card needs a device and capacity requirement, and internal upgrades need a planned project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my Alexa setup and peripheral interests, but often confuse familiar products with something I currently need."
}
